{"entryId":"1170","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1170:1","sourceSha256":"01409a47163d6855bff366963846017f97fb92d1e76edc4375711010ba7c732d","englishSha256":"f263d4fc371fdec0d0afbefc25171f697f62a6a0da7521788c26abda494d02cc","citations":[{"id":"1170:1:citation-01","he":[6,23],"en":[9,32],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_42a.3"},"reference":"Berakhot 42a:3","assessment":"The title is Rav in the Berakhot household account and Ketubot’s transmission from or before Shmuel. Shabbat tracts preserve Rabbi in this witness. A bare name only is asserted in Heilprin.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 42a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_42a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ketubot 60a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_60a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 108b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_108b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1170:1:citation-02","he":[39,72],"en":[52,82],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_34a.8"},"reference":"Avodah Zarah 34a:8","assessment":"The gloss quotes the exact son of Rava form, then conjectures a missing generation. The Bavli passage and Bava Batra keep their different extant forms.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 34a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_34a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 143b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_143b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1],"holds":[{"raw":"אולי צ\"ל רב חביבא בריה דרב יוסף בר רבא","reason":"The separate passages have different genealogical wording. Keep the gloss’s proposal qualified.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 34a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_34a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 143b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_143b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The two genealogies remain distinct. Berakhot and Ketubot use Rav for Yehudah, while Shabbat has Rabbi.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 34a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_34a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 143b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_143b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Berakhot 42a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_42a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ketubot 60a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_60a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 108b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_108b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
